WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.662
Most estates owe no federal estate tax.

2
00:00:03.662 --> 00:00:05.541
The threshold is high,

3
00:00:05.541 --> 00:00:08.790
and for 2026 it is fifteen million dollars

4
00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:10.600
per person.

5
00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:14.191
Only the amount above that is taxed,

6
00:00:14.191 --> 00:00:18.600
at rates that top out at forty percent.

7
00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:20.452
For married couples,

8
00:00:20.452 --> 00:00:24.018
portability lets a surviving spouse use the unused

9
00:00:24.018 --> 00:00:26.829
part of the first spouse's exemption,

10
00:00:26.829 --> 00:00:31.600
but you generally have to file a return to elect it.

11
00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:35.562
Gifts during life count against the same exemption,

12
00:00:35.562 --> 00:00:38.472
but each year you can give a set amount

13
00:00:38.472 --> 00:00:40.966
per person without it counting.

14
00:00:40.966 --> 00:00:45.100
For 2026, that is nineteen thousand dollars.

15
00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:48.818
Some states have their own estate or inheritance tax,

16
00:00:48.818 --> 00:00:51.147
often with much lower thresholds.

17
00:00:51.147 --> 00:00:53.600
Check your state's rules.

18
00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:56.910
Thresholds change with law and inflation,

19
00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.607
so check the year.

20
00:00:58.607 --> 00:01:01.970
Planning matters even if you are under them,

21
00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:05.600
for income tax basis and for control.

22
00:01:05.825 --> 00:01:08.276
Not sure where you stand?

23
00:01:08.276 --> 00:01:12.145
Let's look at your numbers together.
